    title: The Thirteenth Test / Evidence case
    question: Which explanation fits all three signed records?
    clueNodes:
    - n22
    - n9
    - n19
    clues:
    - "The Directorate\u2019s budget funds both the response team and the resistance relay."
    - A test plan names your first contract before you accepted it.
    - Success criteria score the replacement operator, not the service outage.
    answers:
    - id: accident
      title: The records disagree because of an ordinary clerical error.
      feedback: A clerical error does not explain the matching signed authorizations and their order.
      correct: 0
    - id: insider
      title: A lone outsider forged every record after the event.
      feedback: The independent receipt and earlier signatures rule out a single later forgery.
      correct: 0
    - id: rehearsal
      title: The resistance and its handler were part of a succession test.
      feedback: The Directorate cultivated both its defenders and its opposition. Your contracts were part of a succession test.
